CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Strongly Reciprocal
CERN-OHL-S-2.0

Preamble
CERN has developed this licence to promote collaboration on the hardware
designs of products, like the creative commons and open source software
licences do for their respective fields.

1. Definitions
1.1 'Licence' means this CERN-OHL-S.
1.2 'Source' means information such as design materials, schematics, PCB
layouts, bill of materials and documentation which can be used to make, test,
operate or maintain a Product.
1.3 'Covered Source' means Source that is released subject to this Licence.
1.4 'Product' means any tangible physical object made using the Source.

2. Grant of Rights
2.1 You may copy and distribute verbatim copies of the Source.
2.2 You may modify the Source and distribute the modified Source, provided that
the modified Source is licensed under this Licence (CERN-OHL-S v2).
2.3 You may manufacture, run, test and distribute Products based on the Source,
provided that you make available the corresponding Source under this Licence.
